{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/811115-fingerprint-faking-gift-this-a-homid-glasswalker-or-bonegnawer-thing","id":811115,"title":"Fingerprint faking Gift, this a homid, glasswalker, or bonegnawer thing...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-18T07:52:58-08:00","id":811115,"title":"Fingerprint faking Gift, this a homid, glasswalker, or bonegnawer thing...","content":"was thinking of a gift that can perfectly fake fingerpints fool automated scanners and mislead the police...this a gnawer glasswalker or homid thing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T08:07:03-08:00","id":811128,"title":"","content":"It is a homid thing since it addresses technology but isn't overly fitting with bone gnawers. Glass Walker would be possible, too - also Ragabash.<br /> <br /> Oddly enough, the only gift that works like that is (on lower levels) a Red Talon gift, that allows to remove elements from crime scenes, that would lead to the supernatural. Besides that, Doppelganger might include fingerprints","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T13:31:29-08:00","id":811296,"title":"","content":"I'd concur with just going with Homid with the base effect described. That said, it could easily be tweaked thematically with minimal mechanical changes to fit more with specific Tribes or even as heinrich mentioned, the Ragabash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T07:36:21-08:00","id":811790,"title":"","content":"The best place to start is with the Red Talon gift that covers up supernatural activity, this gives you a level. I think this niche type gift would work well for Ragabash, Glass Walkers (particularly the Wise Guy camp), Bone Gnawers and in light of the growing paranoia in wake of the terrorist attacks in Europe and the U.S. I could even see the Silent Striders. .<br /> <br /> Best guess at what this sort of gift would look like:<br /> <br /> Rank 1 this gift when activated alters the finger prints of the Garou this makes identification impossible when the prints are compared. Spend a gnosis point and roll wits plus larceny/streetwise difficulty is 6. Note I might if I was developing this into a gift tie the roll to either jam technology or the gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T21:21:58-08:00","id":816653,"title":"","content":"I agree that it could be Homid, or even Ragabash, depending on how you wanted it to work.<br /> <br /> A simple success could make your fingerprints random/untraceable. There may already be a gift that covers your tracks/leaves no marks where you walked.<br /> <br /> <i>Suggestion:</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Counterfeit Prints</b><br /> <i>Rank 1 Homid, or Ragabash.</i><br /> <br /> Either shake a target's hand, or have a copy of the target's finger prints in your possession.<br /> Spend 1 Gnosis. Roll Perception + Subterfuge, difficulty 7.<br /> Success allows the user to have replicated the unique identifiable patterns of their target on their own hands (palms, fingers, fingertips) that they had access to for one hour. At the end of that hour, the prints return to normal. If the Garou only has the finger prints, they do not gain palm prints. Touching the target's hand gives them full access to that hand's full prints.<br /> For the next 24 hours the Garou may spend 1 Gnosis to have the prints remain, or return for one hour in succession, or at a time up to half their Gnosis per day.<br /> <br /> This gift is taught by a Mocking Bird spirit. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}